L61: La Table de Peutinger
L63-L65: Name and identification details: Tabula Peutingeriana, Austrian National Library, Department of Manuscripts, Autographs and Closed Collections (Cod. 324).
L67-L69: The map has 11 parchment segments; the diagram for the cursus publicus road system uses symbols for cities according to importance.
L70: The Table is described as the only ancient map preserved to our time representing the Roman cursus publicus communication network. It covers Roman provinces and territories conquered by Alexander in the East; it is a medieval parchment facsimile of a manuscript used in antiquity.
L71: The document informs historians of Roman administration and economy and guides archaeologists studying remains of Roman roads and imperial sites.
L72: It was not intended to represent regions like a geographic map; it shows the structure and network of the cursus publicus, omits the sea and is oriented west-east, like a metro diagram.
L75-L83: Image copyright Austrian National Library Cod. 324; registered/submitted 2007 by Austria.
L87-L91: Document type Maps; reference documents include nomination forms.
L92-L124: Collection and media gallery, related themes, page footer.

